5. "Source" should contain the exact page number, and the sentences that you referred to. Never Never paraphrase.

6. All questions should include additional information such as laboratory data, imaging findings, and EKG. You have to mention detailed numerical results when it comes to laboratory data.
If you think exams aren’t necessary, you can just “Exam” blank.

7. keep chief complaint and purpose blank.

8. These are questions that Korean medical students will be solving to achieve a medical license.
Options should be very tricky enough to make students who even studied hard can get stuck between the tricky options.

9. You have to make questions regarding various chief complaints, but never forget that you only have to refer to the PDFs that I attached. 

10. Make sure that you create diverse and distinctive questions. Some questions might share the same diseases, but the options, exams and the questions should be different.
